Package: HarmonicRegression
Type: Package
Title: Harmonic Regression to One or more Time Series
Version: 1.99999999
Date: 2024-09-16
Author: Pål O. Westermark
Maintainer: Pål O. Westermark <westermark@fbn-dummerstorf.de>
Description: Fits the first harmonics in a Fourier expansion to one or more time
    series, either using least squares methods or robust nonparametric methods. 
    Nuisance variables (such as batch or trend) are supported. Computed values 
    include estimates of amplitudes and phases, as well as confidence intervals 
    and p-values for the null hypothesis of independent identically distributed 
    random variability. Additionally, p-values are computed for the null 
    hypothesis of the first harmonic (normalized by random variability) exceeding 
    a threshold value: this can be used for detecting absence of (strong) 
    rhythmicity. 
